{
  "title": "Z-Transform Tables",
  "intro": "Common z-transform pairs with their regions of convergence, the properties, and the one-sided rules used to solve difference equations, in one place to look things up.",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "text": "Throughout, $X(z) = \\sum_{n=-\\infty}^{\\infty} x[n] z^{-n}$, $u[n]$ is the unit step and $\\delta[n]$ the unit impulse. A formula is only half an answer: the same $X(z)$ can belong to different signals, and the region of convergence (ROC) says which. The page The Region of Convergence (#/math/z-transform/region-of-convergence) explains why."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Transform pairs"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Signal $x[n]$",
        "Transform $X(z)$",
        "ROC"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "$\\delta[n]$",
          "$1$",
          "every $z$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\delta[n-k]$",
          "$z^{-k}$",
          "every $z$ except $0$ (if $k > 0$) or $\\infty$ (if $k < 0$)"
        ],
        [
          "$u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{1}{1 - z^{-1}}$",
          "$|z| > 1$"
        ],
        [
          "$-u[-n-1]$",
          "$\\frac{1}{1 - z^{-1}}$",
          "$|z| < 1$"
        ],
        [
          "$n\\,u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{z^{-1}}{(1 - z^{-1})^2}$",
          "$|z| > 1$"
        ],
        [
          "$a^n u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{1}{1 - a z^{-1}}$",
          "$|z| > |a|$"
        ],
        [
          "$-a^n u[-n-1]$",
          "$\\frac{1}{1 - a z^{-1}}$",
          "$|z| < |a|$"
        ],
        [
          "$n\\, a^n u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{a z^{-1}}{(1 - a z^{-1})^2}$",
          "$|z| > |a|$"
        ],
        [
          "$-n\\, a^n u[-n-1]$",
          "$\\frac{a z^{-1}}{(1 - a z^{-1})^2}$",
          "$|z| < |a|$"
        ],
        [
          "$(n+1)\\, a^n u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{1}{(1 - a z^{-1})^2}$",
          "$|z| > |a|$"
        ],
        [
          "$a^n$ for $0 \\le n \\le N-1$, else $0$",
          "$\\frac{1 - a^N z^{-N}}{1 - a z^{-1}}$",
          "every $z$ except $0$"
        ],
        [
          "$r^{|n|},\\ 0 < r < 1$",
          "$\\frac{1 - r^2}{(1 - r z^{-1})(1 - r z)}$",
          "$r < |z| < 1/r$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\cos(\\omega_0 n)\\, u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{1 - \\cos\\omega_0\\, z^{-1}}{1 - 2\\cos\\omega_0\\, z^{-1} + z^{-2}}$",
          "$|z| > 1$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\sin(\\omega_0 n)\\, u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{\\sin\\omega_0\\, z^{-1}}{1 - 2\\cos\\omega_0\\, z^{-1} + z^{-2}}$",
          "$|z| > 1$"
        ],
        [
          "$r^n \\cos(\\omega_0 n)\\, u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{1 - r\\cos\\omega_0\\, z^{-1}}{1 - 2r\\cos\\omega_0\\, z^{-1} + r^2 z^{-2}}$",
          "$|z| > r$"
        ],
        [
          "$r^n \\sin(\\omega_0 n)\\, u[n]$",
          "$\\frac{r\\sin\\omega_0\\, z^{-1}}{1 - 2r\\cos\\omega_0\\, z^{-1} + r^2 z^{-2}}$",
          "$|z| > r$"
        ]
      ],
      "caption": "Pairs that differ only in the ROC (the right- and left-sided rows) share a formula."
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "text": "To turn a table entry into a pole-zero plot, multiply top and bottom by the highest power of $z$: $\\frac{1}{1 - a z^{-1}} = \\frac{z}{z - a}$, a zero at 0 and a pole at $a$."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Properties"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "text": "Here $x[n] \\leftrightarrow X(z)$ with ROC $R_x$, and $y[n] \\leftrightarrow Y(z)$ with ROC $R_y$. Properties as Geometry (#/math/z-transform/properties) shows what each one does to the plane."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Property",
        "Signal",
        "Transform",
        "ROC"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Linearity",
          "$a\\,x[n] + b\\,y[n]$",
          "$a X(z) + b Y(z)$",
          "contains $R_x \\cap R_y$"
        ],
        [
          "Time shift",
          "$x[n - k]$",
          "$z^{-k} X(z)$",
          "$R_x$, except possibly $0$ or $\\infty$"
        ],
        [
          "Scaling by an exponential",
          "$a^n x[n]$",
          "$X(z/a)$",
          "$|a| R_x$"
        ],
        [
          "Modulation",
          "$e^{j\\omega_0 n} x[n]$",
          "$X(e^{-j\\omega_0} z)$",
          "$R_x$"
        ],
        [
          "Conjugation",
          "$x^*[n]$",
          "$X^*(z^*)$",
          "$R_x$"
        ],
        [
          "Time reversal",
          "$x[-n]$",
          "$X(1/z)$",
          "$1/R_x$"
        ],
        [
          "Convolution",
          "$x[n] * y[n]$",
          "$X(z)\\, Y(z)$",
          "contains $R_x \\cap R_y$"
        ],
        [
          "Multiplying by n",
          "$n\\, x[n]$",
          "$-z \\frac{dX(z)}{dz}$",
          "$R_x$"
        ],
        [
          "First difference",
          "$x[n] - x[n-1]$",
          "$(1 - z^{-1}) X(z)$",
          "contains $R_x \\cap \\{|z| > 0\\}$"
        ],
        [
          "Running sum",
          "$\\sum_{k=-\\infty}^{n} x[k]$",
          "$\\frac{X(z)}{1 - z^{-1}}$",
          "contains $R_x \\cap \\{|z| > 1\\}$"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "One-sided transform: initial conditions"
    },
    {
      "type": "prose",
      "text": "The one-sided (unilateral) transform $X^+(z) = \\sum_{n=0}^{\\infty} x[n] z^{-n}$ starts the sum at $n = 0$. Its shift rule carries the values before $n = 0$ along, which is how a difference equation with initial conditions is solved. The initial-value rule holds for any signal, since $X^+$ ignores $n < 0$ (for the two-sided $X(z)$ it needs $x[n] = 0$ for $n < 0$), and the final-value rule holds only when every pole of $(z - 1)X^+(z)$ is inside the unit circle."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Rule",
        "Signal",
        "One-sided transform"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Delay by one",
          "$x[n-1]$",
          "$z^{-1} X^+(z) + x[-1]$"
        ],
        [
          "Delay by two",
          "$x[n-2]$",
          "$z^{-2} X^+(z) + z^{-1} x[-1] + x[-2]$"
        ],
        [
          "Advance by one",
          "$x[n+1]$",
          "$z X^+(z) - z\\, x[0]$"
        ],
        [
          "Initial value",
          "$x[0]$",
          "$\\lim_{z \\to \\infty} X^+(z)$"
        ],
        [
          "Final value",
          "$\\lim_{n \\to \\infty} x[n]$",
          "$\\lim_{z \\to 1} (z - 1) X^+(z)$"
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
